root = "D:/Github_Codes/class-hosting-platform-github/"


def sub(p, a, b):
    f = root + p
    s = open(f, encoding="utf8").read()
    assert a in s, (p, a[:60])
    open(f, "w", encoding="utf8").write(s.replace(a, b, 1))


sub("starter/rules/AGENTS.md", "- **If your editor has the `class-platform` tools:** use `project_status`, `push_project` and `pull_project` (ask the student first, then `confirm=true`; `dry_run=true` only looks). Otherwise run the npm commands.",
    "- **If your editor has the `class-platform` tools:** use `project_status`, `push_project`, `pull_project` and `project_auto` (ask the student first, then `confirm=true`; `dry_run=true` only looks). Otherwise run the npm commands.\n- **Saving the project automatically (ask ONCE).** When `status` says \"Project files: NOT saved on the platform yet\", ask the student exactly once: \"Save a copy of your project files on the platform, so you can use them on other computers? Your teacher can read them, and I will also save them after every deploy.\" If they say yes, call `push_project` with `confirm=true` (that first push also turns on saving after every deploy); if they say no, call `project_auto` with `enabled=false` and do not ask again. After that every `deploy` saves the files by itself and you do not need to push; the student can change their mind with `project_auto`.")
